{
 "note": "Mutants of what a dedicated server's room says about where its players can be reached, for tools/mutate.py (docs/TESTING.md, 'Mutation checks'): a server's room sends no address or port of any player (the Start of the lobby, the Start that a machine from nothing is given, the Start in a restart record), a game that plays through a server opens no listener for the other players, and a game on the local network still opens one and is named to the others. A guest's session with migration off ignores what another guest says over a link, a game in a server's room dials no endpoint, and the listener of a game on the local network keeps at most 8 silent connections for 5 s each. Against test_lobby (N4.5c), test_server (S3.99 for the Start of a room's machines and the record, S3.99b for every message that the server sends), test_rejoin (RJ1.30) and test_netgame (N3.9, host migration; N3.12b, the listener), test_lockstep (N2.34b) and test_rejoin (RJ1.31). Run from the checkout with a configured build folder: python3 tools/mutate.py tests/data/server_room_no_addresses_mutants.json --keep-going --jobs 1. Every mutant must be caught.",
